  "track.animation.m.aas.s.create.explain": "`remember { AnimateAsState(target, …) }` creates an `Animatable(0f)`; the remember block sets `updating = false`, so the first time there is NO `SideEffect` and no animation: the value starts exactly at the target.",
  "track.animation.m.aas.ev.create": "remember creates AnimateAsState",
  "track.animation.m.aas.s.read.title": "Reading state.value",
  "track.animation.m.aas.s.read.explain": "The returned value is a `State<Float>`; reading it reads `animatable.value` (via `asState()`), a snapshot state.",
  "track.animation.m.aas.ev.read": "Reading state.value",
  "track.animation.m.aas.s.end.first.title": "The end: no job at all",
  "track.animation.m.aas.s.end.first.explain": "The first time only builds things; nothing runs.",
  "track.animation.m.aas.ev.end.first": "The end: no job at all",
  "track.animation.m.aas.s.recompose.title": "Recompose with target 100 → SideEffect calls update()",
  "track.animation.m.aas.s.recompose.explain": "After composition applies, `SideEffect` calls `state.update(100f, …)`. Because 100 differs from `animatable.targetValue` (0), the animation must (re)start.",
  "track.animation.m.aas.ev.recompose": "Recompose with target 100 → SideEffect calls update()",
  "track.animation.m.aas.s.recomposeSame.title": "Recompose with the same target 100",
