  "track.animation.m.segment.title": "One Transition, three children, and when currentState changes",
  "track.animation.m.segment.overview": "The `Collapsed ↔ Expanded` card from the Value-based page. One `Transition` drives three children: alpha (a 150 ms tween), color (a 300 ms tween), height (a spring, about 400 ms in the model). Three situations: a normal expansion; changing back to Collapsed mid-way; and a `MutableTransitionState` that starts different from its target.",
  "track.animation.m.segment.wrapup": "`updateTransition` groups several values under one state. When the target changes, every child starts at the same time, each with its own spec.\n`currentState` stays the old state until EVERY child is done, and only then becomes the target; `isRunning` tells you whether any child is still running. Changing the target mid-way turns every child around together. To run as soon as it enters composition, use a `MutableTransitionState` with an initial state different from the target.\nRule of thumb: one state, many values, starting together: that is `updateTransition`.",
  "track.animation.m.segment.simp.1": "The spring's duration (about 400 ms) and the 150/300/450 ms marks are illustrative; the model does not draw each child's curve.",
  "track.animation.m.segment.simp.2": "When turning around mid-way, the model does not say what `segment` becomes; the docs only guarantee that children adjust towards the new target and `currentState` changes when done.",
  "track.animation.m.segment.ctl.hint": "Run \"expand\" and watch currentState; then try changing back mid-way.",
