  "track.animation.m.segment.s.end.expand.explain": "As long as the slowest child.",
  "track.animation.m.segment.ev.end.expand": "The end: current = Expanded after 400 ms",
  "track.animation.m.segment.s.end.reverse.title": "The end: back to Collapsed",
  "track.animation.m.segment.s.end.reverse.explain": "Changing your mind mid-way does not make values jump.",
  "track.animation.m.segment.ev.end.reverse": "The end: back to Collapsed",
  "track.animation.m.segment.s.end.mutable.title": "The end: current = Expanded",
  "track.animation.m.segment.s.end.mutable.explain": "`MutableTransitionState` also has `isIdle` to tell when it is done.",
  "track.animation.m.segment.ev.end.mutable": "The end: current = Expanded",
  "track.animation.m.segment.co.mutable": "The KDoc: the `MutableTransitionState` variant allows an initial state different from the target, so the Transition starts as soon as it enters composition; and it can be recreated to restart on purpose. [[src:an-transition-src]]",
  "track.animation.m.segment.co.adjust": "The KDoc: when the target changes, the Transition automatically starts or adjusts course for all its children towards the new values. [[src:an-transition-src]]",
  "track.animation.m.segment.co.current": "The KDoc: `currentState` is always the initialState until the transition is finished; then it is set to targetState. [[src:an-transition-src]]",
  "track.animation.m.segment.co.end.expand": "A Transition also has `isRunning`, `segment` (the initial and target state of the ongoing run) and `currentState`. [[src:book-kunneth]]",
  "track.animation.m.segment.co.end.mutable": "This is the right way for an element to \"fade in on appearing\" (C1 bug 1). [[src:an-transition-src]]",
  "track.animation.cap.segment": "The state on the left gives the Transition in the middle its target; the three children on the right run together, each with its own spec. The metrics count running children and time.",
  "track.animation.c3.sim.animation.segment": "currentState and the children",
