  "track.animation.m.exitlife.co.stillThere": "The KDoc: content is only removed after all exit animations (built-in and custom) have finished. [[src:an-av-src]]",
  "track.animation.m.exitlife.co.waitAll": "The KDoc: AnimatedVisibility waits until ALL enter/exit animations finish before it considers itself idle. [[src:an-av-src]]",
  "track.animation.m.exitlife.co.outside": "The docs: animations outside the Transition (such as animate*AsState) are not tracked, so content may be removed before they finish. [[src:an-composables]]",
  "track.animation.m.exitlife.co.end.builtin": "Defaults: fadeIn + expandIn on enter, fadeOut + shrinkOut on exit; inside Row/Column there are tailored defaults. [[src:an-av-src]]",
  "track.animation.m.exitlife.co.end.custom": "Custom animations created on `AnimatedVisibilityScope.transition` run alongside the built-in ones and are waited for. [[src:an-av-src]]",
  "track.animation.m.exitlife.co.end.outside": "To act after the exit finishes (remove data, sequential animations), the KDoc suggests the variant taking a `MutableTransitionState`. [[src:an-av-src]]",
  "track.animation.cap.exitlife": "The visible flag on the left drives AnimatedVisibility; top right is the content still in composition, bottom right is when it has been removed.",
